.TH "INSTALLEVENT.ADDROUTES" "3JS" "July 4, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
InstallEvent.addRoutes \- InstallEvent: addRoutes() method
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]addRoutes()\f[B]\f[R] method of the
\f[CR]InstallEvent\f[R] interface specifies one or more static routes,
which define rules for fetching specified resources that will be used
even before service worker startup.
This allows you to, for example, bypass a service worker in cases where
you always want to fetch a resource from the network or a browser
\f[CR]Cache\f[R], and avoids the performance overhead of unnecessary
service worker cycles.
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
addRoutes(routerRules)
.EE
.SS Parameters
.TP
\f[B]routerRules\f[R]
A single object, or an array of one or more objects, representing rules
for how certain resources should be fetched.
Each \f[CR]routerRules\f[R] object contains the following properties:
.RS
.TP
\f[B]condition\f[R]
An object defining one or more conditions that specify which resources
should match this rule.
The following properties can be included; if multiple properties are
used, a resource must meet all specified conditions to match the rule.
.RS
.TP
\f[B]not\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
A \f[CR]condition\f[R] object defining conditions that must explicitly
\f[B]not\f[R] be met to match the rule.
Conditions defined inside a \f[CR]not\f[R] condition are mutually
exclusive with other conditions.
.TP
\f[B]or\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
An array of \f[CR]condition\f[R] objects.
One set of these defined conditions must be met to match the rule.
Conditions defined inside an \f[CR]or\f[R] condition are mutually
exclusive with other conditions.
.TP
\f[B]requestMethod\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
A string representing the HTTP method a request should be sent by for it
to match the rule, such as \f[CR]\(dqget\(dq\f[R],
\f[CR]\(dqput\(dq\f[R], or \f[CR]\(dqhead\(dq\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]requestMode\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
A string representing the mode a request should have for it to match the
rule, for example \f[CR]\(dqsame\-origin\(dq\f[R],
\f[CR]\(dqno\-cors\(dq\f[R], or \f[CR]\(dqcors\(dq\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]requestDestination\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
A string representing the destination of a request, i.e., what content
type should be requested, for it to match the rule.
Examples include \f[CR]\(dqaudio\(dq\f[R], \f[CR]\(dqdocument\(dq\f[R],
\f[CR]\(dqscript\(dq\f[R], and \f[CR]\(dqworker\(dq\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]runningStatus\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
An enumerated value representing the required running status of the
service worker for a request to match the rule.
Values can be \f[CR]\(dqrunning\(dq\f[R] or
\f[CR]\(dqnot\-running\(dq\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]urlPattern\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
A \f[CR]URLPattern\f[R] instance, or a \f[CR]URLPattern()\f[R]
constructor \f[CR]input\f[R] pattern representing the URLs that match
the rule.
Regular expression capturing groups are not allowed, so
\f[CR]URLPattern.hasRegExpGroups\f[R] must be \f[CR]false\f[R].
.RE
.TP
\f[B]source\f[R]
An enumerated value or an object specifying the source from which
matching resources will be loaded.
Possible enumerated values are:
.RS
.TP
\f[B]\(dqcache\(dq\f[R]
Resources will be loaded from a browser \f[CR]Cache\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]\(dqfetch\-event\(dq\f[R]
Resources will be loaded via the service worker\(cqs \f[CR]fetch\f[R]
event handler.
This can be combined with the \f[CR]\(dqrunningStatus\(dq\f[R] condition
to load resources from a service worker if it is running and fall back
to a static route on the network if it is not.
.TP
\f[B]\(dqnetwork\(dq\f[R]
Resources will be loaded from the network.
.TP
\f[B]\(dqrace\-network\-and\-fetch\-handler\(dq\f[R]
Attempts are made to load resources from the network and the service
worker\(cqs \f[CR]fetch\f[R] event handler simultaneously.
Whichever one completes first is used.
The \f[CR]source\f[R] value can also be set to an object containing a
single property, \f[CR]cacheName\f[R], the value of which is a string
representing the name of a browser \f[CR]Cache\f[R].
Matching resources will be loaded from this specific named cache if it
exists.
.RE
.RE
.SS Return value
A \f[CR]Promise\f[R] that fulfills with \f[CR]undefined\f[R].
.SS Exceptions
.TP
\f[B]TypeError\f[R] \f[B]DOMException\f[R]
Thrown if one or more of the rules objects inside \f[CR]routerRules\f[R]
is invalid, or has a \f[CR]source\f[R] value of
\f[CR]\(dqfetch\-event\(dq\f[R] when the associated service worker does
not have a \f[CR]fetch\f[R] event handler.
Also thrown if you try to combine \f[CR]or\f[R] with another condition
type.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Route specific requests to the network if the service worker is not running
In the following example, URLs that start with \f[CR]/articles\f[R] are
routed to the network if the service worker is not currently running:
.IP
.EX
addEventListener(\(dqinstall\(dq, (event) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  event.addRoutes({
    condition: {
      urlPattern: \(dq/articles/*\(dq,
      runningStatus: \(dqnot\-running\(dq,
    },
    source: \(dqnetwork\(dq,
  });
});
.EE
.SS Route form post requests to the network
In the following example, \f[CR]POST\f[R] requests to a form are sent
directly to the network and bypass the service worker:
.IP
.EX
addEventListener(\(dqinstall\(dq, (event) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  event.addRoutes({
    condition: {
      urlPattern: \(dq/form/*\(dq,
      requestMethod: \(dqpost\(dq,
    },
    source: \(dqnetwork\(dq,
  });
});
.EE
.SS Route certain image type requests to a named cache
In the following example, the browser \f[CR]Cache\f[R] named
\f[CR]\(dqpictures\(dq\f[R] is used for fetching files with extensions
of \f[CR].png\f[R] or \f[CR].jpg\f[R]:
.IP
.EX
addEventListener(\(dqinstall\(dq, (event) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  event.addRoutes({
    condition: {
      or: [{ urlPattern: \(dq*.png\(dq }, { urlPattern: \(dq*.jpg\(dq }],
    },
    source: {
      cacheName: \(dqpictures\(dq,
    },
  });
});
.EE
.RS
.PP
\f[B]Note:\f[R] If the cache does not exist, the browser defaults to
using the network so that the requested resources can still be obtained
provided the network is available.
.RE
.PP
You can\(cqt combine \f[CR]or\f[R] with another condition \(em this
results in a \f[CR]TypeError\f[R].
If for example you wanted to match files with extensions of
\f[CR].png\f[R] or \f[CR].jpg\f[R] but only when the
\f[CR]requestMethod\f[R] is \f[CR]get\f[R], you\(cqd need to specify two
separate conditions:
.IP
.EX
addEventListener(\(dqinstall\(dq, (event) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  event.addRoutes(
    {
      condition: {
        urlPattern: \(dq*.png\(dq,
        requestMethod: \(dqget\(dq,
      },
      source: {
        cacheName: \(dqpictures\(dq,
      },
    },
    {
      condition: {
        urlPattern: \(dq*.jpg\(dq,
        requestMethod: \(dqget\(dq,
      },
      source: {
        cacheName: \(dqpictures\(dq,
      },
    },
  );
});
.EE
